<<<============teleop=============>>>
TERMINAL 0 — STOP OLD CONTAINERS (only once)
docker stop bumblebot_container
docker rm bumblebot_container

TERMINAL 1 — START DOCKER & ROSCORE
docker run -it \
  --name bumblebot_container \
  --net=host \
  -e DISPLAY=$DISPLAY \
  -v /tmp/.X11-unix:/tmp/.X11-unix \
  -v ~/BumbleBot_WS:/root/BumbleBot_WS \
  --device=/dev/ttyUSB0 \
  --device=/dev/ttyUSB1 \
  --device=/dev/ttyUSB2 \
  ros_noetic_custom:latest /bin/bash


Inside container:

cd ~/BumbleBot_WS
source devel/setup.bash
roscore


Keep this running.

TERMINAL 2 — START TELEOP SYSTEM

Open a new terminal:

docker exec -it bumblebot_container bash


Inside container:

1. Source workspace
cd ~/BumbleBot_WS

source devel/setup.bash

2. Launch your full teleop system

(test_teleop.launch must exist in bringup/launch/teleop/)

roslaunch /root/BumbleBot_WS/src/bringup/launch/teleop/test_teleop.launch


You should now see:

/twist_to_motors started
/teleop_keyboard started
/diff_tf started
RPLIDAR running...


Good.

TERMINAL 3 — RUN KEYBOARD CONTROL

Open new terminal:

docker exec -it bumblebot_container bash


Inside container:

source ~/BumbleBot_WS/devel/setup.bash
rosrun teleop_twist_keyboard teleop_twist_keyboard.py


You must see:

Reading from keyboard and publishing to /cmd_vel
i = forward
j = rotate left
l = rotate right
, = backwards


Now the robot WILL MOVE.




